-- title:
--   varpi A is prime when κ ⊗_R A is a domain
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $A$ a commutative $R$-algebra, and $\kappa$ a field that is an $R$-algebra. Let $\varpi \in R$ and assume: the kernel of the structure map $R \to \kappa$ is exactly the principal ideal $(\varpi)$; the ideal $(\varpi)$ is a maximal ideal of $R$; and the tensor product $\kappa \otimes_R A$ is a domain (in Mathlib's sense, so in particular it is nontrivial and has no zero divisors). The conclusion is that the ideal of $A$ generated by the image $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,_R^A(\varpi)$, that is the ideal $\varpi A$, is a prime ideal of $A$; by Mathlib's convention this includes the assertion $\varpi A \neq A$. No finiteness, flatness or Noetherian hypothesis on $A$ is imposed.
--
--   This is the standard descent of integrality along a base change to the residue field: a domain hypothesis upstairs, over a field $\kappa$ whose kernel over $R$ is the maximal ideal $(\varpi)$, forces $\varpi A$ to be prime. It is applied in the treatment of modular curves, in [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb_mem_chartAlgFin_of_forall_coeff_of_isIntegral_adjoin_jq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.coeffEmb_mem_chartAlgFin_of_forall_coeff_of_isIntegral_adjoin_jq) and in [`ModularCurve.isPrime_span_algebraMap_chartAlgFin_xHFunctionField_top_of_natCast_ne_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isPrime_span_algebraMap_chartAlgFin_xHFunctionField_top_of_natCast_ne_zero), where $R$ is local with uniformiser $\varpi$ and $\kappa$ is a field extension of its residue field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ideal_isPrime_span_algebraMap_of_isDomain_tensor.lean

